Your missing weapon class is quarterstaff.  Your Quest artifact
is the Staff of Misspelling and it is argably the best artifact in
the game for a healer.  Save the slots for it.

So a general strategy for healers -

Advance knife enough to make it usefull.  Gather more knives
for throwing to practice skill even though they don't machine-gun.
Let's call it Basic early on (so no action since that's where you
start) and Skilled later.  Expert if you decide to go without
artifacts and use a crysknife.

Advance unihorn to Basic or Skilled early on.  Not enough
point to advancing it past Skilled

Practice with any quaterstaff to prepare for your Quest artifact.
Eventually you will want to be Expert at it?

Practice with darts to machine-gun.  Eventual expert?

Ignore any other weapon except artifacts.  Advance your crowning
gift to Basic and use it a lot.

Dart to Basic 1 slot.  Unihorn to Basic 1 slot.  Staff to Basic
1 slot. Healing spell to Basic 1 slot.  Crowning gift to Basic 1
slot.  So far the total is 6 slots.

Dart, knife, unihorn, staff, healing to Skilled total if 9 slots
grand total of 15 and it's time to do the Quest.

Dart, healing staff (or knife for no artifact game) to Expert total
of 8 slots grand total 23 and if you get to 30 you'll have 7 gravy
skill slots for style points if I did the arithmatic right.

No way the items will come to you in that order, so the actual
